/// Index of the mechanical family; its libraries are the sub-packages catalog,
/// thread, fastener, drill, driver, gears and joint.

// Mechanical Library (mechanical)
//
// Shared base for the mechanical family. The libraries themselves live in
// sub-packages by subject:
//
//   import "mechanical/catalog";   // the standard sizes, one row per size
//   import "mechanical/thread";    // ISO 68-1 thread profiles and pitches
//   import "mechanical/fastener";  // ISO screws, nuts, washers, dowels
//   import "mechanical/drill";     // generalized holes as a stack of features
//   import "mechanical/driver";    // screwdriver bits and screwdrivers
//   import "mechanical/gears";     // involute spur and bevel gears
//   import "mechanical/joint";     // joints: the interface between parts in one call
//
// They share one list of standard sizes. mechanical/catalog holds it — one row
// per nominal diameter carrying the thread pitch and every fastener dimension
// for that size — so a thread and the screw cut with it cannot disagree about
// which sizes exist. Anything here that is sized by a standard thread diameter
// reads its numbers from there.
//
// The convention across the family: a part is a solid and a feature that
// receives one is a VOID SOLID, which the caller subtracts. So a screw is
// min'd into the scene and a hole is subtracted from the part:
//
//   max(plate, -drill.hole([drill.chamfer(7.0, 0.5), drill.thru(6.6)], 0))
//
// Doc convention follows builtin/base.gsl: `///` lines are public docs.
